Even though the internet is very, very large,

53
00:02:34,280 --> 00:02:36,080
we're working with text and we're also

54
00:02:36,080 --> 00:02:37,440
filtering it aggressively.

55
00:02:37,440 --> 00:02:40,840
So we end up with about 44 terabytes in this example.

56
00:02:40,840 --> 00:02:44,560
So let's take a look at what this data looks like

57
00:02:44,560 --> 00:02:47,200
and what some of these stages also are.

58
00:02:47,200 --> 00:02:49,360
So the starting point for a lot of these efforts

59
00:02:49,360 --> 00:02:51,320
and something that contributes most of the data

60
00:02:51,320 --> 00:02:55,280
by the end of it, is data from CommonCroll.

61
00:02:55,280 --> 00:02:56,760
So CommonCroll is an organization

