00:03:36,080 --> 00:03:38,480
that happens in these stages.

78
00:03:38,480 --> 00:03:42,400
So the first thing here is something called URL filter.

79
00:03:42,400 --> 00:03:44,440
So what that is referring to is that there

80
00:03:44,440 --> 00:03:49,780
is these block lists of basically URLs

81
00:03:49,780 --> 00:03:52,360
that are or domains that you don't want

82
00:03:52,360 --> 00:03:53,700
to be getting data from.

83
00:03:53,700 --> 00:03:56,600
So usually this includes things like malware websites,

84
00:03:56,600 --> 00:03:59,900
spam websites, marketing websites, racist websites,

85
00:03:59,900 --> 00:04:01,740
adult sites, and things like that.

86
00:04:01,740 --> 00:04:03,620
So there's some of the different types of websites

87
00:04:03,620 --> 00:04:06,020
that are just eliminated at this stage

88
00:04:06,020 --> 00:04:08,710
because we don't want them in our dataset.

89
00:04:08,710 --> 00:04:10,750
The second part is text extraction.

90
00:04:10,750 --> 00:04:12,270
You have to remember that all of these web pages,

91
00:04:12,270 --> 00:04:15,470
this is the raw HTML of these web pages that are being saved

92
00:04:15,470 --> 00:04:16,870
by these crawlers.

93
00:04:16,870 --> 00:04:19,520
So when I go to inspect here,

94
00:04:19,520 --> 00:04:22,120
This is what the raw HTML actually looks like.

