606
00:32:23,000 --> 00:32:27,160
The maximum context length here was 1,024 tokens.

607
00:32:27,160 --> 00:32:31,640
So it is when we are sampling chunks of windows

608
00:32:31,640 --> 00:32:33,760
of tokens from the data set.

609
00:32:33,760 --> 00:32:36,280
We're never taking more than 1,024 tokens.

610
00:32:36,280 --> 00:32:37,960
And so when you are trying to predict the next token

611
00:32:37,960 --> 00:32:42,000
in a sequence, you will never have more than 1,024 tokens

612
00:32:42,000 --> 00:32:45,190
kind of in your context in order to make that prediction.

613
00:32:45,190 --> 00:32:47,390
Now, this is also tiny by modern standards.

614
00:32:47,390 --> 00:32:50,470
Today, the context lengths would be a lot closer

615
00:32:50,470 --> 00:32:53,720
to a couple hundred thousand,

616
00:32:53,720 --> 00:32:55,040
or maybe even a million.

617
00:32:55,040 --> 00:32:56,560
And so you have a lot more context,

618
00:32:56,560 --> 00:32:58,480
a lot more tokens in history.

619
00:32:58,480 --> 00:32:59,960
And you can make a lot better prediction

620
00:32:59,960 --> 00:33:02,980
about the next token in a sequence in that way.

